== words
-- builtin member of an array [length]
```novus
method length(): integer
```

The number of elements.
-- free builtin function [readFile]
```novus
method readFile(string path): string
```

Reads a whole file; the empty string when it cannot be opened.
-- keyword [method]
```novus
method
```

Declares a method: `method name(type parameter): Type { ... }`. The parameter list and the return type are optional; `method main` is the entry point.
-- keyword var [var]
```novus
var
```

Declares a variable: `var name = value` or `var name: Type = value`. Redeclaring a name in the same block assigns to it.
-- primitive type [float]
```novus
float
```

A floating point number. Aliases: `double`, `doub`.
-- annotation [Deprecated]
```novus
@Deprecated{text="...", since="..."}
```

Marks a method as deprecated: the first call prints a runtime warning with `text` and `since` (the version).
-- std module name [strings]
```novus
std module strings
```

The standard module `strings` has 20 functions and constants. Import it with `import strings`.
-- package name [geo]
```novus
package geo
```

1 file, 3 functions and constants.
whitespace: (none)
== ambiguity
-- a call defined in two packages [shared]
**Ambiguous**: defined in more than one package
- `left.shared(): integer` (package `left` · a.nv)
- `right.shared(): integer` (package `right` · b.nv)
Write the call qualified, for example `left.shared(...)`.
